Stops `FolderState::revert` from taking the wants at reverted paths off
the list and re-deriving them from their received entries once the
restoring wants are in place (the revert half of 34363b1). A want that
was resolved against the discarded record, such as a conflict's `M`
that folds in the local version revert throws away, then stays as it
was, and every version arriving behind it is deferred as concurrent with
it (DESIGN.md §8.3 step 2, §7.5).

Since draft 57 made a revert's move to the trash a want of its own, a
path whose file revert trashes gets a new want from the revert either
way, so the engine test of the conflict's `M` no longer reaches the fix.
The unit test below does: the restoring want at the path is the one
re-derived from A's received version.

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_want_at_a_reverted_path_is_rederived_from_the_received_entry
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_restoring_want_inherits_no_refusals

